  "title": "The 3n+1 conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Let $f(n) = 3n+1$ if $n$ is odd and $\\frac{n}{2}$ if $n$ is even. Let $f(1) = 1$. Assume we start with some number $n$ and repeatedly take the $f$ of the current number. Prove that no matter what the initial number is we eventually reach $1$.",
